import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# Stacks 070S part (3): `(id_{τ,étale})^*𝓖` as a sheafified sections rule

Let `B` be a big fppf site, `S` a scheme it contains, `τ` one of the five topologies refining
the étale one, and `𝓖` an **arbitrary** sheaf of `𝒪`-modules on the small étale site `S_étale`.
**Stacks 070S part (3)** says that the inverse image `(id_{τ,étale})^*𝓖` along the morphism of
ringed sites `id_{τ,étale} : ((Sch/S)_τ, 𝒪) ⟶ (S_étale, 𝒪)` is the `τ`-sheafification of the
étale sheaf `(f : T → S) ↦ Γ(T, f_small^*𝓖)` on `(Sch/S)_τ`, for `f_small : T_étale ⟶ S_étale`
the morphism of ringed small étale sites of **Stacks 070R (2)**.  That is
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.baseSmallEtalePullbackIsoSectionsSheafification`.

`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.sectionsSheafTauPresheafOfModules` is the sections rule, built over
the big *étale* presentation `BigEtaleOver B S hS` of the category of `S`-schemes.  This file
re-reads it over the big *fppf* presentation `BigFppfOver B S hS`, which is the same category
under another spelling, and over the structure sheaf
`AlgebraicGeometry.FibredSite.baseRingStructureSheaf` of the big `τ`-site — the coefficient sheaf
over which `(id_{τ,étale})^* = AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.smallEtaleToBaseModulePullback`
takes its values.

## The route

`CategoryTheory.SheafOfModules.pullbackIso` presents `(id_{τ,étale})^*𝓖` as the
`τ`-sheafification of the *presheaf*-level inverse image `P` of `𝓖` along the inclusion of the
small étale site, so what has to be produced is a locally bijective comparison
`γ : P ⟶ (f : T → S) ↦ Γ(T, f_small^*𝓖)`.  It is
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.smallEtaleSectionsGamma`, the transpose of the localization map
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.sectionsSheafTauLocApp`, which on sections over an étale `V / S` is
the unit along `ε_v` followed by restriction along the diagonal `V → V ×_S V`.

Local bijectivity of `γ` at an object `T` is read off the small étale site of the scheme of `T`.
There the sections rule at `T` *is* `Γ(T, f_small^*𝓖)` — the same group by definition, nothing is
transported — and three comparisons are in play:

* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.sectionsSheafTauTheta`, the comparison `θ` from the
  presheaf-level inverse image `P_f` of `𝓖` along `ε_f` to the sheaf `f_small^*𝓖`.  It is the
  sheafification unit followed by an isomorphism
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.sectionsSheafTauTheta_eq`), hence locally bijective;
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.smallEtaleSectionsKappa`, the comparison `κ : P_f ⟶ i_T^{-1}P`,
  which is surjective in every component
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.smallEtaleSectionsKappa_surjective`) because the pullback of a
  presheaf of modules is generated by the image of the unit and every index `W / S ⟶ V / S` of a
  generator comes from a `W ⟶ T ×_S V`;
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.smallEtaleSectionsRho`, the comparison `ρ'` of the sections rule
  with the sections of `f_small^*𝓖`.

They are tied together by `κ ≫ i_T^{-1}γ = θ ≫ ρ'`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.smallEtaleSectionsKappa_comp_gamma`), whose content on a
generator is the identity
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.sectionsSheafTauRho_unitSectionsApp`.  Étale covering sieves
produced on the small étale site of the scheme of `T` are transferred to the big `τ`-site by
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.coverPreserving_smallEtaleOverFunctor`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.smallEtaleSectionsPresheafOfModules`: the presheaf of
  `𝒪`-modules `(f : T → S) ↦ Γ(T, f_small^*𝓖)` on the big `τ`-site of `S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.smallEtaleSectionsLoc`: the localization map
  `𝓖 ⟶ (id_{τ,étale})_*` of that presheaf.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.smallEtaleSectionsGamma`: **the comparison `γ`.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.smallEtaleOverFunctor`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.smallEtaleOverRingMap` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.nuNatTrans`: the functor presenting `i_T` of Stacks 021F on the
  big `τ`-site, the identity `i_T^{-1}𝒪 = 𝒪`, and the comparison `i_T ∘ f_small ⟹ i_S` of
  Stacks 021I (4).
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.smallEtaleSectionsKappa` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.smallEtaleSectionsRho`: **the comparisons `κ` and `ρ'`.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.baseSmallEtalePullbackIsoSectionsSheafification`:
  **Stacks 070S part (3)**, with `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.baseSmallEtaleIsoSectionsEtale`
  and `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.baseSmallEtaleIsoSectionsFppf` its instances at
  `τ = étale` and `τ = fppf`.  The two in between, `.baseSmallEtaleIsoSectionsSmooth` and
  `.baseSmallEtaleIsoSectionsSyntomic`, are in
  `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Descent/AssociatedModulePullbackBigToSmallEtale.lean`, where
  the continuity of the inclusion of the small étale site first becomes an instance at those
  two `τ`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.smallEtaleSectionsKappa_comp_gamma`: **the key identity**
  `κ ≫ i_T^{-1}γ = θ ≫ ρ'`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.smallEtaleSectionsKappa_surjective`: **`κ` is surjective.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.coverPreserving_smallEtaleOverFunctor`: **étale covering sieves
  transfer** to the big `τ`-site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isLocallySurjective_smallEtaleSectionsGamma` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isLocallyInjective_smallEtaleSectionsGamma`: **`γ` is locally
  bijective**, and therefore
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isIso_baseSheafification_map_smallEtaleSectionsGamma`.

## Implementation notes

`BigEtaleOver B.toBigEtaleSite S hS` and `BigFppfOver B S hS` are the same category, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.FibredSite.baseRingStructureSheaf B S hS τ` and the structure presheaf
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.bigEtaleOverRing B.toBigEtaleSite S hS` are the same presheaf of
rings — in both cases global functions on the underlying scheme — but
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.toBigEtaleSite` is a definition that instance search does not
unfold, so the two spellings have to be crossed once by an ascription.  That is all this file
does; it is the same device as
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.smallEtaleToFppf`, which ascribes the target of the inclusion of
the small étale site.

That crossing is *not* what is expensive here.  Both halves of it elaborate under the default
budget: `(smallEtaleToFppf B S hS).map k = k.hom` is a reflexivity, and so is the identification
of the sections of `CategoryTheory.PresheafOfModules.pushforward` of the sections rule with the
sections of the sections rule at the included object.  What is expensive is the identification of
the two *functors*: that the presheaf of abelian groups underlying
`CategoryTheory.PresheafOfModules.pushforward` of a presheaf of modules is the restriction along
the functor of its underlying presheaf.  Checked at these concrete presheaves it unfolds
`CategoryTheory.SheafOfModules.pullback` — a left adjoint obtained from an adjunction by
`Classical.choose`, whose unfolding carries no information — tens of thousands of times, and with
it the pullback cones of the schemes involved.

`CategoryTheory.PresheafOfModules.homToPushforwardPresheaf` removes that cost: Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.PresheafOfModules.pushforwardCompToPresheaf` already proves the identification for
an arbitrary functor and an arbitrary presheaf of modules, where it is cheap, so stating it once
in that generic form lets the declarations below be built at the restricted-presheaf spelling and
transported, rather than each re-deciding the identification at its own concrete presheaf.  The
transport is definitional, so the components are unchanged: `smallEtaleSectionsRho_app` is still
a reflexivity.

The same discipline is what keeps the rest of the file inside the default budget, and in each
case the fix is to fix the spelling *before* the unifier is asked to guess it.

* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.smallEtaleSectionsRho_smul` states the linearity of `ρ'` at the
  spelling of its two factors.  Every crossing it needs is cheap on its own; what was not was
  elaborating the two factors *against* the semilinearity condition of
  `CategoryTheory.PresheafOfModules.homMk`, where the scalar of the second factor is still a
  metavariable and solving it descends into the pullback cones.
* `CategoryTheory.PresheafOfModules.homToPushforwardComp` and its two companions do for the
  *iterated* pushforward what `CategoryTheory.PresheafOfModules.homToPushforwardPresheaf` does
  for the underlying presheaf.  Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.PresheafOfModules.pushforwardComp`
  identifies pushing forward along `F` and then `G` with pushing forward along `F ⋙ G`
  generically, where it is cheap; at the concrete presheaves here the same identification
  unfolds `CategoryTheory.SheafOfModules.pullback` again.  So the key identity and the generator
  identity it rests on are both stated on the far side of that transport, which is the identity
  function.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.eq_zero_of_sectionsSheafTauMap_eq_zero` leaves the objects of
  the big site as parameters.  At the concrete pair the statement has to identify the sections of
  the sections rule with the sections of `f_small^*𝓖` over the final object, which is the same
  unfolding once more; over parameters it is immediate.

## Related

The narrow case `𝓖 = 𝓕ᵃ`, for `𝓕` quasi-coherent on the scheme `S`, is
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.smallEtalePullbackIsoSectionsSheafification` (module
`SmallEtalePullbackSectionsSheaf` under `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/EtaleCohomology/`),
where Stacks 03FH (2) removes the small-étale inverse image from the sections rule altogether;
part (1) of the source is
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.baseAssociatedModuleIsoSections`.

